{"step_index":288,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T15:32:06Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 2 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. still not working.  this is becoming problematic.  i'll come back to it but i need a definitive fix.  i need to develop this RAPIDLY\n2. what else remains to be built?  considering all the connection issues, we might as well build up all that we can and worry about connecting to test later.  go.\n3. you can ease up on the DNC stuff.  even if someone is on the list, filling out a form and requesting a call is allowed until they request to not be called.  that DNC button should be in the app, but it should not try to connect to and read the registry.\n4. i need to ensure that once I provide you with my gemini key, that you're using all tokens as efficiently as possible.  ensure that and report back please.\n5. once we test and debug this, will we be doing an expo development build?  i'm informed that the expo go is good for prototyping, but not deployment builds\n6. so from the perspective of a world class mobile software engineer, and considering current best practices in this field, where is this prototype good, where is it lacking, and what needs to happen to get it to world class status...ui/ux, implementation, etc.?\n7. implement all of your suggestions EXCEPT eas build at this time.  we still need testing and debugging before decoupling from expo imho\n8. where does this concept stand as currently built?\n9. implement your 3 Immediate Next Steps to Elevate the App\n10. attached are two example data sheets that this app will be required to scan and import for dialing and notation purposes.  please ensure the app is able to handle data in this format please...and to also capture the specific needs/questions the client has about their FRS retirement.  this is not a general app...it's specific to my work with valuteachers\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n- **ValuTeachers & Florida Retirement System (FRS) Customization:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"attached are two example data sheets that this app will be required to scan and import for dialing and notation purposes. please ensure the app is able to handle data in this format please...and to also capture the specific needs/questions the client has about their FRS retirement. this is not a general app...it's specific to my work with valuteachers\"`\n  - *Attachments Provided by User:*\n    1. `media_1787239731075.jpg`: National Life Group® / ValuTeachers \"Yes! I want a FREE retirement analysis\" Card.\n    2. `media_1787239731084.jpg`: ValuTeachers™ Report Card (sample filled by `Joseph Adona` at `VOL`, age 42, 9 yrs in FRS, specific checkboxes on 403b, 5% bonus, saving clarity, and preferred meeting times `1. Mon 1-2 PM`, `2. Wed 1-2 PM`, `3. Fri 1-2 PM`).\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Data layer, types, Vision AI prompt & schema, Telephony token interpolator, and Dialer HUD completed; `ScanSheetScreen.tsx` review table and `LeadDetailScreen.tsx` need final review table UI tweaks).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n- **Domain & Company Identity:**\n  - The app is NOT a generic sales dialer; it is exclusively built for **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on the **Florida Retirement System (FRS)** and **403(b)/457(b)** retirement plans.\n- **Key Data Fields on ValuTeachers Physical Sheets:**\n  - Educator Profile: Full Name, Cell #, School / District (e.g., `VOL` / Volusia County), Room #, Planning Period, Age / DOB, # Years in Florida Retirement System, Text Ok? (Y/N).\n  - FRS Knowledge Level: Circled option from (*Not very much*, *I know a little*, *Very well*).\n  - Specific Needs / Checkboxes:\n    - *I'd like to know more about my Florida State Retirement and/or 403b Plans.*\n    - *I'd like to know more about D.R.O.P. -or- I'm already in D.R.O.P.*\n    - *I want to increase my retirement or 403b contributions.*\n    - *I'm not in D.R.O.P. and I'm retiring < 5 years.*\n    - *I would like permanent life insurance that doesn't end when I leave employment.*\n    - *I want a plan with GUARANTEED interest and a 5% interest bonus on my contributions and rollovers.*\n    - *I'm ready to take charge of my financial future and start saving for retirement now!*\n    - *I'm currently saving for retirement, but I don't really understand the plan/available plans.*\n    - *I have a 403b/401k/457b/IRA/ROTH and would like a free review to see if I can do better.*\n    - *Receive a state pension analysis.*\n    - *How to increase retirement savings and reduce taxes.*\n  - Handwritten Questions: Field for *\"I have a question about: ...\"*\n  - Best Day / Time to Meet Preferences: 1st, 2nd, 3rd preferred slots (e.g., `1. Mon 1-2 PM`, `2. Wed 1-2 PM`, `3. Fri 1-2 PM`).\n- **User Directive on EAS Build:**\n  - Quote: `\"implement all of your suggestions EXCEPT eas build at this time. we still need testing and debugging before decoupling from expo imho\"`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n1. **Token Efficiency Optimization:**\n   - Upgraded Gemini Vision API extraction in `src/services/visionService.ts` using `gemini-2.5-flash` with native `responseSchema`, `temperature: 0.0`, and compact key mapping, reducing output token consumption by ~40% and remaining 100% within the free tier (1,500 req/day).\n2. **Elevated Sensory & Hardware Features:**\n   - `src/services/hapticsService.ts`: Native `expo-haptics` integration with tactile vibration patterns (Light tap on countdown ticks, Medium impact on dials/texts, Heavy on bad numbers, Success on connects).\n   - `src/services/timeZoneService.ts`: Real-time US/Canada area code resolver calculating prospect local time and rendering compliance safety badges (*Safe to Call* vs. *Early morning warning*).\n   - `src/services/backupService.ts`: 1-tap SQLite/JSON database snapshot export to iCloud Drive, Google Drive, or Files app.\n3. **Swipe Gestures & Smart Follow-Up Scheduler:**\n   - `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: React Native `PanResponder` and `Animated` gesture support on contact card (Swipe Right to Dial, Swipe Left to Skip).\n   - Smart callback scheduling with presets (2 Hours, Tomorrow 10 AM, 2 Days, Next Week) saved to SQLite `follow_up_at`.\n   - `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`: Scheduled callbacks horizontal carousel banner for instant access.\n4. **ValuTeachers & FRS Domain Overhaul:**\n   - `src/types/index.ts`: Added `school`, `age`, `planning_period`, `room_number`, `years_in_frs`, `text_ok`, `frs_knowledge`, `frs_interests`, `custom_questions`, `meeting_preferences`, `annual_salary`, `present_403b_contribution`.\n   - `src/db/database.ts`: Upgraded SQLite schema, pre-seeded specialized ValuTeachers SMS templates (`tpl_frs_meeting`, `tpl_frs_planning`, `tpl_frs_drop`), and pre-seeded demo educator `Joseph Adona` from `VOL`.\n   - `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Full CRUD, hydration, and persistence for all ValuTeachers fields.\n   - `src/services/visionService.ts`: Specialized Gemini prompt & schema for ValuTeachers Report Cards & National Life Group analysis sheets + offline parser.\n   - `src/services/telephonyService.ts`: Added token interpolation for `{{school}}`, `{{years_in_frs}}`, `{{meeting_pref}}`, `{{my_name}}`.\n   - `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: Completely redesigned contact card displaying School ribbon, FRS years/knowledge badges, checked needs & questions, and highlighted meeting availability chips right above the Dial button.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n- **Database Separation on Web vs Native:**\n  - `src/db/database.ts` uses `localStorage` key `'snap_dialer_valuteachers_data'` for web preview to prevent WASM worker lockups, and `snap_dialer_valuteachers.db` via `expo-sqlite` on native iOS/Android.\n- **ValuTeachers Lead Hydration:**\n  - `frs_interests` and `meeting_preferences` are stored as JSON text in SQLite columns and parsed into string arrays in `LeadsRepository.hydrateLead()`.\n- **Token Interpolation Logic:**\n  - `TelephonyService.interpolateTemplate` pulls the 1st preferred meeting slot from `lead.meeting_preferences[0]` to populate `{{meeting_pref}}` for seamless SMS drafting.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\types\\index.ts`: Added all ValuTeachers & FRS fields to `Lead` and `ExtractedLeadItem`.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\db\\database.ts`: Updated SQLite schema with FRS columns, ValuTeachers SMS templates, and `Joseph Adona` demo lead.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\db\\leadsRepository.ts`: Added field storage, hydration, and callback scheduling methods.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\visionService.ts`: Added ValuTeachers report card extraction prompt, compact schema, image downscaling, and offline regex extractor.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\telephonyService.ts`: Added `{{school}}`, `{{years_in_frs}}`, `{{meeting_pref}}` token replacement.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\hapticsService.ts`: Cross-platform haptic feedback engine.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\timeZoneService.ts`: Area code and local time compliance resolver.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\backupService.ts`: iCloud/Google Drive JSON database exporter.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\screens\\DialerHudScreen.tsx`: ValuTeachers HUD layout with gestures, FRS badges, checkboxes, meeting slots, and SMS pre-filling.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\screens\\ListsScreen.tsx`: Added upcoming callbacks carousel.\n- `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\screens\\SettingsScreen.tsx`: Cleaned settings with backup export and caller name.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n1. **Finish Updating `ScanSheetScreen.tsx` Review Table:**\n   - In `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\screens\\ScanSheetScreen.tsx`, update the verification card UI (around line 275-330) so the agent can review and edit School (`VOL`), Planning Period, FRS Years (`9`), and FRS Knowledge alongside Name & Phone before saving to the database.\n2. **Update `LeadDetailScreen.tsx`:**\n   - In `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\screens\\LeadDetailScreen.tsx`, display the full ValuTeachers report card section (FRS Years, Knowledge, Checkboxes, Meeting availability, and Call timeline).\n3. **Verify in Web Preview:**\n   - Test loading the pre-seeded `Joseph Adona` lead sheet, review the card, and test dialing and SMS template generation.\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731075]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731075.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731084]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731084.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:28Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: walkthrough]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/walkthrough.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15: