{"step_index":299,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T15:32:49Z","content":"The application has been customized specifically for **ValuTeachers** and the **Florida Retirement System (FRS)**.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built & Customized for ValuTeachers:\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      VALUTEACHERS / FRS PROSPECTING HUD                          │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  🎓 Joseph Adona • (386) 212-3234 • jradona@volusia.k12.fl.us                    │\n│  🏫 VOL (Volusia County) • Room 204 • 3rd Period Planning                        │\n│                                                                                  │\n│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ 🎓 9 Yrs in FRS   │  Age: 42   │  FRS Knowledge: \"I know a little\"         │  │\n│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n│                                                                                  │\n│  REPORT CARD NEEDS & HOT-BUTTONS:                                                │\n│  ✓ Florida State Retirement and/or 403b Plans                                    │\n│  ✓ Guaranteed interest & 5% bonus on contributions/rollovers                     │\n│  ✓ Saving for retirement but needs plan clarity                                  │\n│                                                                                  │\n│  REQUESTED MEETING AVAILABILITY:                                                 │\n│  [1. Mon 1-2 PM]  [2. Wed 1-2 PM]  [3. Fri 1-2 PM]                              │\n│                                                                                  │\n│  [             DIAL (386) 212-3234 (OR SWIPE RIGHT)             ]                │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Capabilities Now Live:\n\n1. **Dual-Card AI Vision Pipeline ([`src/services/visionService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/visionService.ts)):**\n   - Tuned specifically for both formats you uploaded:\n     1. **ValuTeachers Report Cards** (extracts school, cell, email, planning period, circled FRS knowledge, checked interests, custom questions, and preferred meeting times).\n     2. **National Life Group / ValuTeachers Free Retirement Analysis Cards** (extracts 403b/457b checkboxes, tax reduction, salary, and pension analysis requests).\n\n2. **Educator Power Dialer HUD ([`src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx)):**\n   - Displays all educator hot-buttons, years in FRS, and preferred callback windows (*1. Mon 1-2 PM, 2. Wed 1-2 PM, 3. Fri 1-2 PM*) directly above the Dial button.\n\n3. **ValuTeachers 1-Tap SMS Templates ([`src/db/database.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/database.ts) & [`src/services/telephonyService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/telephonyService.ts)):**\n   - Auto-fills educator details and availability:\n     > *\"Hi Joseph, this is Alex with ValuTeachers. I received your FRS Report Card from VOL. I see you requested to connect on Mon 1-2 PM to review your Florida State Retirement & 403(b) options. Does that time still work for you?\"*\n\n4. **Pre-Loaded Sample Data:**\n   - Seeded with an exact replica of the **Joseph Adona** report card you uploaded for instant testing.\n\n---\n\n### How to Test:\nRefresh your browser at `http://localhost:8081` (or run `npx expo start --web`) to test the new ValuTeachers HUD and report card parsing!"}
{"step_index":300,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T15:40:16Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\ndid you address the following deficiency you identified earlier?  if not, please do so:\n\nDocument Ingestion & Vision Pipeline\r\nThe Issue: The prototype sends raw captured photos directly to the API without on-device edge cropping or pre-compression.\r\nWhy it matters: A 48-megapixel iPhone photo is 8MB–12MB. Uploading that over cellular data wastes bandwidth and adds 3–5 seconds of latency.\r\nWorld-Class Solution:\r\nNative Document Scanner: Use react-native-document-scanner-plugin or iOS VisionKit to automatically detect paper edges, flatten perspective, enhance contrast, and remove shadows on-device.\r\nOn-Device Image Downsampling: Resize the flattened document to 1600 \r\n×\r\n× 1200 JPEG (quality 0.75) before transmission, reducing upload size from 10MB to <250KB and cutting API response time to under 1.2 seconds.\r\nOffline On-Device OCR Fallback: Integrate Apple Vision (VNRecognizeTextRequest) on iOS and Google ML Kit on Android so basic printed rosters can be parsed 100% on-device with zero internet connection.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-20T11:40:16-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":301,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T15:40:16Z","thinking":"**Addressing the Deficiency**\n\nI've been concentrating on the document ingestion pipeline. Specifically, I'm now implementing edge cropping and pre-compression steps on the device before API transmission. The goal is to address the identified deficiency by optimizing the initial image handling and resource management. I'm focusing on ensuring it integrates seamlessly into the workflow.\n\n\n**Refining Image Processing**\n\nI'm now focusing on optimizing image handling for both web and mobile. I've confirmed that the native side downsamples and compresses images to under 250KB using `expo-image-manipulator`. Now, I'm verifying that HTML Canvas on the web performs equivalent downscaling/compression to match the mobile performance. Integration of `react-native-document-scanner-plugin` is next on my list.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\package.json","toolAction":"Viewing package.json","toolSummary":"View package.json"}}]}
